@startuml wasm-umbrella-deployment
' The JavaScript umbrella topology: one @vinary-tree/javascript-runtime runtime owns
' one coherent resource table per selected runtime path — native N-API by
' default, browser WASM and WASI Preview 1 behind explicit subpath exports —
' and every lightweight project facade verifies the runtime identity before
' accepting a resource, so raw handles can never cross incompatible
' instances. WASI receives only explicitly preopened directories.
' Color: shared JavaScript runtime + facades = engines purple #E1BEE7 / #F3E5F5
'   (#6A1B9A); runtime instances (sandbox/trust surfaces) = trust-boundary
'   #FFCDD2 / tint #FFEBEE (#B71C1C); the per-runtime resource table =
'   VtResource green #DCEDC8 (#33691E); host filesystem grant = leased
'   memory #FFECB3 (#FF6F00).
' Source of truth: the standalone javascript-runtime/package.json (exports),
'   native.mjs / wasm.mjs / wasi-runtime.mjs (runtimeIdentity, preopens),
'   runtime-factory.mjs (requireDictionary/requireWfst identity guard),
'   docs/bindings/wasm-topology.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam node {
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #F9A825
}

title Umbrella deployment — one runtime, one resource table, identity-guarded facades

node "Host JavaScript process (Node or browser)" as HOST {
  rectangle "Project facades (typed, lightweight)\n@vinary-tree/liblevenshtein · @vinary-tree/libdictenstein\n@vinary-tree/lling-llang · @vinary-tree/duallity" as FACADES #F3E5F5

  rectangle "@vinary-tree/javascript-runtime — shared JavaScript runtime" as UMBRELLA #E1BEE7 {
    rectangle "'.' default export\nnative N-API addon\nidentity: vinary-tree-node-napi-v1\n(all four Rust components\nstatically linked)" as NAPI #FFEBEE
    rectangle "'./wasm' export\nbrowser WebAssembly instance\nidentity: vinary-tree-wasm-v1\n(no persistent backend)" as WASM #FFEBEE
    rectangle "'./wasi' export\nWASI Preview 1 instance\nidentity: vinary-tree-wasi-preview1-v1" as WASI #FFEBEE
    rectangle "one resource table per runtime\n(dictionaries, transducers, WFSTs\nshared <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> in-process)" as TABLE #DCEDC8
  }
}

rectangle "Host filesystem\n(embedder-chosen preopen map,\ndefault: /workspace → cwd)" as FS #FFECB3

FACADES -[#6A1B9A]-> UMBRELLA : resolve one runtime path,\nthen share it
FACADES .[#B71C1C].> TABLE : identity guard: a resource is accepted\nonly if resource.runtimeIdentity matches\nthe facade's resolved runtime
NAPI -[#33691E]-> TABLE
WASM -[#33691E]-> TABLE
WASI -[#33691E]-> TABLE
WASI -[#FF6F00]-> FS : preopens only — no ambient\nfilesystem; persistent ARTrie\nlives at preopened paths only

note bottom of WASM #FFEBEE
  A WASM trap kills the instance, not the host —
  the sandbox isolation is part of WebAssembly's
  formal semantics (Haas et al. 2017). Wave-W3
  hardening (LLEV-B4) converts the runtime crate's
  remaining panic-class sites to status/JsError.
end note

note bottom of NAPI #FFEBEE
  Node consumers install no shared library and
  configure no loader path: the prebuilt addon
  statically contains interop + all four projects.
  Wave-W3 hardening (LLEV-B12) binds the N-API
  symbols the type declarations already promise.
end note
@enduml
